1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,651
Episode Eighty-Three covered event-driven flows and the transactional outbox.

2
00:00:06,651 --> 00:00:12,179
Performance work without a method becomes random tuning theater.

3
00:00:12,179 --> 00:00:18,225
Users feel latency percentiles — not average CPU on a quiet afternoon.

4
00:00:18,225 --> 00:00:24,444
Java gives you JFR, async profilers, GC logs, and Micrometer — use them.

5
00:00:24,444 --> 00:00:28,331
Fix the hottest path first — then re-measure.

6
00:00:28,331 --> 00:00:33,514
Today — a performance playbook from symptom to verified fix.

7
00:00:33,514 --> 00:00:35,790
Episode Eighty-Four.

8
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:38,180
Performance Playbook.

9
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:41,895
Start with measurement — never with a hunch.

10
00:00:41,895 --> 00:00:47,299
Define the SLO — p95 latency, error rate, throughput under load.

11
00:00:47,299 --> 00:00:51,858
Reproduce with realistic data volumes and concurrency.

12
00:00:51,858 --> 00:00:56,924
Capture RED metrics — rate, errors, duration — per endpoint.

13
00:00:56,924 --> 00:01:01,568
Add traces for the slow requests — see where time goes.

14
00:01:01,568 --> 00:01:05,958
Without a baseline, you cannot claim an improvement.

15
00:01:05,958 --> 00:01:09,588
Find the bottleneck before changing code.

16
00:01:09,588 --> 00:01:14,988
CPU-bound — profile methods — hot loops, JSON, crypto, regex.

17
00:01:14,988 --> 00:01:20,123
IO-bound — watch DB time, remote calls, thread pool waits.

18
00:01:20,123 --> 00:01:26,320
Allocation pressure — GC logs and allocation profilers tell the story.

19
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:31,808
Lock contention — thread dumps and JFR synchronization events.

20
00:01:31,808 --> 00:01:37,120
One primary bottleneck at a time — resist shotgun refactors.

21
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:40,544
Application-level fixes that often win.

22
00:01:40,544 --> 00:01:45,459
Cut N-plus-one queries — fetch joins or DTO projections.

23
00:01:45,459 --> 00:01:51,429
Cache correct hot reads — with invalidation from Episode Eighty-One.

24
00:01:51,429 --> 00:01:56,257
Shrink payloads — less JSON, fewer columns, pagination.

25
00:01:56,257 --> 00:02:02,051
Reuse connections and HTTP clients — connection setup is not free.

26
00:02:02,051 --> 00:02:08,810
Move heavy work off the request thread — async or queues when product allows.

27
00:02:08,810 --> 00:02:11,232
Runtime and platform levers.

28
00:02:11,232 --> 00:02:17,112
Size heaps and pick collectors from GC evidence — Episode Sixty-Two.

29
00:02:17,112 --> 00:02:22,820
Tune thread and pool sizes to measured concurrency — not folklore.

30
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:27,836
Warm up JIT before load tests that claim peak performance.

31
00:02:27,836 --> 00:02:33,025
Watch container CPU throttling — limits can fake a slow app.

32
00:02:33,025 --> 00:02:39,252
Native images and AOT help startup — steady-state still needs profiling.

33
00:02:39,252 --> 00:02:41,423
Verify like a scientist.

34
00:02:41,423 --> 00:02:45,674
One change, then re-run the same load scenario.

35
00:02:45,674 --> 00:02:49,292
Compare p95 and p99 — not only averages.

36
00:02:49,292 --> 00:02:55,533
Watch error rate — a faster endpoint that five-hundreds is not a win.

37
00:02:55,533 --> 00:03:00,961
Keep a short performance note — what changed, what improved.

38
00:03:00,961 --> 00:03:07,654
Automate a smoke performance check in CI for critical paths when feasible.

39
00:03:07,654 --> 00:03:09,673
Three common mistakes.

40
00:03:09,673 --> 00:03:15,087
One — optimizing before measuring — classic premature work.

41
00:03:15,087 --> 00:03:21,969
Two — load testing with tiny datasets — missing real index and GC behavior.

42
00:03:21,969 --> 00:03:26,465
Three — celebrating mean latency while p99 burns.

43
00:03:26,465 --> 00:03:31,236
Also — changing five knobs at once — no attribution.

44
00:03:31,236 --> 00:03:34,448
Method beats folklore — every time.

45
00:03:34,448 --> 00:03:41,353
Interview question — an endpoint's p99 doubled after a release — what do you do?

46
00:03:41,353 --> 00:03:46,877
Confirm blast radius — which endpoint, since when, which region.

47
00:03:46,877 --> 00:03:51,883
Compare metrics and traces before versus after the deploy.

48
00:03:51,883 --> 00:03:56,803
Profile or pull JFR — classify CPU, IO, GC, or lock wait.

49
00:03:56,803 --> 00:04:01,464
Fix the top offender — re-measure under the same load.

50
00:04:01,464 --> 00:04:07,506
Ship with a rollback plan — performance incidents need escape hatches.

51
00:04:07,506 --> 00:04:12,774
Speed is one production virtue — readiness is the checklist.

52
00:04:12,774 --> 00:04:17,339
Episode Eighty-Five — Production Readiness Capstone.

53
00:04:17,339 --> 00:04:22,607
The Season Two finale — ship checklist and staff-level wrap.

54
00:04:22,607 --> 00:04:23,836
See you there.
